# 🚀 .NET Backend Engineering — Level 2

## 3-Month Advanced Backend Mentorship Program

**Duration:** 12 Weeks
**Sprints:** 6
**Sprint Duration:** 2 Weeks
**Project Type:** Production-style Modular Monolith REST API
**Target:** Junior → Advanced Junior / Strong Junior Backend Developer

---

# 🎯 Program Goal

The goal of this program is to move trainees beyond CRUD development and expose them to the engineering practices used when building real backend applications.

By the end of the program, trainees should be able to:

* Design a structured ASP.NET Core Web API.
* Apply Clean Architecture appropriately.
* Model real business rules instead of building CRUD-only endpoints.
* Use CQRS and MediatR for application workflows.
* Build secure APIs using JWT, Refresh Tokens, Claims and Policies.
* Write efficient EF Core queries.
* Handle validation, errors, transactions and concurrency.
* Implement pagination, filtering, searching and sorting.
* Apply caching where appropriate.
* Build background processing.
* Integrate external services.
* Write meaningful Unit and Integration Tests.
* Containerize the application using Docker.
* Build a basic CI pipeline using GitHub Actions.
* Deploy a real backend application.
* Understand the trade-offs behind architectural decisions.

> **The goal is not to teach as many patterns as possible.**
>
> The goal is to teach trainees how to make good backend engineering decisions.

---

# 🏗️ Main Project — TeamFlow

## Project Description

**TeamFlow** is a project and task management platform for teams.

Users can create projects, manage project members, create and assign tasks, track task progress, communicate through comments, receive notifications, and monitor project activity.

The system grows gradually throughout the six sprints.

---

