* ASP.NET Core Identity
* JWT
* Refresh Tokens
* Claims

---

## Task 2 — Project Ownership

A Project must have an owner.

Implement:

```text
User
 ↓
Owned Projects
```

A user should only be able to manage projects they own or are authorized to manage.

---

## Task 3 — Project Membership

Introduce:

```text
ProjectMember
```

Support:

```http
POST   /projects/{id}/members
DELETE /projects/{id}/members/{userId}
GET    /projects/{id}/members
```

Rules:

* Only authorized users can manage members.
* A user cannot be added twice.
* Only existing users can become members.
* Unauthorized users cannot access private project data.

---

## Task 4 — Task Assignment

Extend Task:

```text
AssignedToUserId
```

Implement:

```http
POST   /tasks/{id}/assign
DELETE /tasks/{id}/assign
GET    /tasks/my
```

Rules:

* Assigned user must exist.
* Assigned user must be a project member.
* Only authorized users can assign tasks.

---

## Task 5 — Task Workflow

Introduce:

```csharp
public enum TaskStatus
{
    Todo,
    InProgress,
    Completed,
    Cancelled
}
```

Implement:

```http
PATCH /api/v1/tasks/{id}/status
```

Valid transitions:

```text
Todo → InProgress
Todo → Cancelled

InProgress → Completed
InProgress → Cancelled
```

Invalid transitions must be rejected.

The Entity should protect its own invariants.

---

## Task 6 — Authorization Policies

Create policies such as:

```text
CanManageProject
CanManageTask
CanManageMembers
```

Authorization must consider the actual resource, not only the user's role.

