# 📝 Sprint 5 Tasks

## Task 1 — Global Exception Handling

Implement centralized exception handling.

All unexpected exceptions should produce a consistent:

```text
ProblemDetails
```

Do not expose:

* Stack traces
* Database details
* Internal implementation details

---

## Task 2 — Correlation ID

Every request should have a correlation identifier.

Use it in logs so a request can be traced through the application.

Example:

```text
Request
 ↓
CorrelationId
 ↓
Application
 ↓
Database
 ↓
Logs
```

---

## Task 3 — Structured Logging

Configure Serilog.

Log:

* HTTP Method
* Path
* Status Code
* Execution Time
* Correlation ID
* Exceptions

Log important business actions:

```text
ProjectCreated
TaskCreated
TaskAssigned
TaskCompleted
CommentAdded
```

---

## Task 4 — Notification Queue

Create:

```text
INotificationQueue
```

Implement an in-memory queue using:

```text
Channel<T>
```

Flow:

```text
Task Assigned
      ↓
Queue Notification
      ↓
BackgroundService
      ↓
Process Notification
```

---

## Task 5 — Notification Scenarios

Trigger background notifications for:

* Task Assigned
* Task Completed
* User Added to Project

No external email system is required.

The purpose is learning asynchronous background processing.

---

## Task 6 — External Service

Create a small external-service integration.

Examples:

```text
Notification Provider
Weather Provider
Exchange Rate Provider
```

The important part is not the service itself.

The trainee must learn:

* HttpClientFactory
* Timeout
* CancellationToken
* Failure handling
* Dependency abstraction

---

## Task 7 — Resilience

Handle external service failures.

Example:

```text
External Service
       ↓
     Timeout
       ↓
   Controlled Failure
       ↓
     API continues
```

Introduce retry/circuit-breaker concepts without turning the project into a distributed-systems project.

---

## 🚫 Explicitly Do NOT Add

